{"availability":"available","full":"dillonkearns/elm-graphql","name":"elm-graphql","description":"Autogenerate type-safe GraphQL queries in Elm.","category":"Other","language":"Elm","stars":788,"forks":107,"created":"2017-11-25T17:01:08Z","updated":"2026-02-14T02:47:31Z","license":"BSD-3-Clause","branch":"master","homepage":"https://package.elm-lang.org/packages/dillonkearns/elm-graphql/latest","topics":["elm","graphql"],"demo":"https://dillonkearns.github.io/elm-graphql/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:41.769Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:41.769Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:41.769Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:32:41.769Z","stars":788,"forks":107}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Why use this package over the other available Elm GraphQL packages? This is the only one that generates type-safe code for your entire schema. Check out this blog post, Type-Safe & Composable GraphQL in Elm, to learn more about the motivation for this library. (It's also the only type-safe library with Elm 0.18 or 0.19 support, see this discourse thread).","I built this package because I wanted to have something that:","dillonkearns/elm-graphql is an Elm package and accompanying command-line code generator that creates type-safe Elm code for your GraphQL endpoint. You don't write any decoders for your API with dillonkearns/elm-graphql, instead you simply select which fields you would like, similar to a standard GraphQL query but in Elm. For example, this GraphQL query"],"features":["Gives you type-safe GraphQL queries (if it compiles, it's valid according to the schema),","Creates decoders for you in a seamless and failsafe way, and","Eliminates GraphQL features in favor of Elm language constructs where possible for a simpler UX (for example, GraphQL variables & fragments should just be Elm functions, constants, lets)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dillonkearns/elm-graphql/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"74daf4b87b6ea20aaa8b2df9cc1526e19901effaf09b8742438088ae66fe4c9d","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:41.858Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:41.858Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Why use this package over the other available Elm GraphQL packages? This is the only one that generates type-safe code for your entire schema. Check out this blog post, Type-Safe & Composable GraphQL in Elm, to learn more about the motivation for this library. (It's also the only type-safe library with Elm 0.18 or 0.19 support, see this discourse thread).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dillonkearns/elm-graphql/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"To do that, you will need to use custom code or a package that knows how to communicate over websockets (or whichever protocol) to setup a subscription with your particular framework.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dillonkearns/elm-graphql/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"74daf4b87b6ea20aaa8b2df9cc1526e19901effaf09b8742438088ae66fe4c9d","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dillonkearns/elm-graphql/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:41.859Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-02-14T02:47:31Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dillonkearns/elm-graphql/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:41.859Z","hash":"74daf4b87b6ea20aaa8b2df9cc1526e19901effaf09b8742438088ae66fe4c9d","originalBytes":11171,"storedBytes":11171,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["elm-graphql","elm","dillonkearns","graphql","code","example","package","query","see","examples","import","selectionset","type-safe","generate","install","learn","like","npm","starwars","subscriptions","thank","through","tutorial","using","any","api","generated","humandata","setup","tool","would","above","base","build","command","decoders","demo","dependency","details","exposing","header","how","humanselection","json","